---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Nuclear Fusion"
  description="Two light nuclei repel each other fiercely, and only by slamming them together hard enough to tunnel through that wall do they merge and pour out energy. Every star and every reactor lives or dies on one line: whether the power coming out beats the power leaking away."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="fus" class="fus-canvas" width="1000" height="720"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Scenario</label>
        <div class="seg" id="scenario">
          <button data-s="cold" class="active">Cold gas</button>
          <button data-s="tokamak">Tokamak</button>
          <button data-s="sun">The Sun</button>
          <button data-s="hbomb">H-bomb</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Fuel</label>
        <div class="seg" id="fuel">
          <button data-f="dt" class="active">D-T</button>
          <button data-f="dd">D-D</button>
          <button data-f="dhe3">D-³He</button>
          <button data-f="pp">H (p-p)</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Temperature <b id="tval">0.5 keV</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="temp" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" value="7.4" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>cool</span><span>hot</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Density <b id="nval">1e20 /m³</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="dens" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" value="7.1" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>thin</span><span>stellar</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Confinement time <b id="tauval">1 s</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="conf" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" value="66.9" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>leaky</span><span>trapped</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">Temperature</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">Reactivity ⟨σv⟩</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">Fusion power</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">Wait per nucleus</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">State</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        The box is a portrait, not a headcount: real densities run to 10³² per
        cubic metre. The reactivity, the power balance and the Lawson line are
        computed from the numbers you dial, not from the dots.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start on <b>Cold gas</b>. The nuclei drift and bounce and simply refuse to
      touch. Two positive charges repel, and at ordinary energies they turn back
      long before they meet. Nothing fuses, the reactivity is essentially zero,
      and no amount of waiting changes that. This is why fusion is hard: the fuel
      does not want to burn.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise the <b>temperature</b>. Now the nuclei are moving fast enough that a
      few of them tunnel through the barrier they cannot climb, and fusion
      flashes begin. Watch the reactivity curve on the right climb almost
      vertically: fusion power is savagely sensitive to temperature, which is why
      you need a hundred million degrees before anything useful happens.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch the <b>fuel</b> at a fixed temperature. D-T lights up first and
      brightest: it has the lowest barrier and the fattest cross section, which
      is why every first-generation reactor burns it. D-D and D-³He need it far
      hotter, and plain hydrogen, the star-maker, barely reacts at all.
    </li>
    <li>
      Load <b>Tokamak</b>. Temperature, density and confinement together push the
      triple product <b>n·T·τ</b> across the Lawson line, and the alpha particles
      the fusion throws off now heat the plasma faster than it leaks. The panel
      flips to <b>ignited</b>: the fire feeds itself. That single crossing is the
      goal of every fusion machine ever built.
    </li>
    <li>
      Drop the <b>confinement time</b> back down. The heat escapes faster than
      fusion can replace it and ignition dies, even though nothing about the fuel
      changed. Confinement is the third leg, and the hardest: holding a
      hundred-million-degree gas still, for long enough, without touching it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Load <b>The Sun</b>. Here is the twist: the Sun is not hot by fusion
      standards, only fifteen million degrees, and plain hydrogen at that
      temperature reacts so feebly that a given proton waits <b>billions of
      years</b> to find a partner. Read the wait time. The Sun works not because
      it burns hard but because it is unfathomably large and gravity holds it
      forever. Its core makes less power per cubic metre than a compost heap.
    </li>
    <li>
      Load <b>H-bomb</b>: D-T squeezed to stellar density and heated by a fission
      trigger. Now the reactivity, the density squared and the released energy
      all pile up at once, and the whole charge burns in the time light crosses
      it. Same equation as the Sun and the tokamak, driven off the top of every
      scale.
    </li>
    <li>
      Fusion, a star and a bomb are one process at three settings. What separates
      them is never the physics, only how hot, how dense, and for how long.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equationBar } from '../../../lib/equation';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Fusion as a power balance. The dots in the box are only a portrait of a hot
  // plasma; the physics on the right is computed straight from temperature,
  // density and confinement time. Fusion power goes as n² <σv>, <σv> climbs
  // almost vertically with temperature (tunnelling through the Coulomb barrier),
  // and ignition is the moment the charged fusion products heat the plasma
  // faster than it loses heat. That crossing is the Lawson criterion.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const KB_KEV_K = 1.16045e7; // 1 keV in kelvin
  const J_PER_KEV = 1.602e-16;
  const CBREM = 5.35e-37; // bremsstrahlung constant, W·m³ (per √keV)

  type FuelKey = 'dt' | 'dd' | 'dhe3' | 'pp';
  interface Fuel {
    label: string;
    Gf: number; // Gamow-like exponent (barrier height)
    sv0: number; // reactivity prefactor, m³/s
    E: number; // energy released per reaction, J
    fc: number; // fraction of that energy staying in the plasma (charged products)
    pair: number; // density² prefactor: 1/4 for two species, 1/2 for one
  }
  const FUELS: Record<FuelKey, Fuel> = {
    // Tuned so the reactivities land in the right places and in the right order.
    dt: { label: 'D-T', Gf: 19.9, sv0: 3.87e-18, E: 2.82e-12, fc: 0.2, pair: 0.25 },
    dd: { label: 'D-D', Gf: 31, sv0: 5.0e-18, E: 5.85e-13, fc: 0.66, pair: 0.5 },
    dhe3: { label: 'D-³He', Gf: 34, sv0: 6.0e-18, E: 2.93e-12, fc: 1.0, pair: 0.25 },
    pp: { label: 'H (p-p)', Gf: 33, sv0: 4.9e-36, E: 4.28e-12, fc: 0.98, pair: 0.5 },
  };

  type Scenario = 'cold' | 'tokamak' | 'sun' | 'hbomb';

  const state = {
    fuel: 'dt' as FuelKey,
    T: 0.5, // keV
    n: 1e20, // m⁻³
    tau: 1, // s, energy confinement time
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    gravity: false, // a star: gravity confines and radiation is trapped
    scenario: 'cold' as Scenario,
  };

  /** Reactivity ⟨σv⟩ in m³/s: the tunnelling-through-the-barrier curve. */
  function reactivity(T: number, f: Fuel) {
    if (T <= 0) return 0;
    return f.sv0 * Math.exp(-f.Gf / Math.cbrt(T)) * Math.pow(T, -2 / 3);
  }

  interface Balance {
    sv: number;
    pFus: number; // W/m³
    pAlpha: number;
    pBrem: number;
    pCond: number;
    pLoss: number;
    ignited: boolean;
    Q: number; // fusion power / external heating needed
    tripleProduct: number; // n T τ, keV·s/m³
    tripleThreshold: number;
    waitYears: number; // mean time for one nucleus to react
  }

  function balance(): Balance {
    const f = FUELS[state.fuel];
    const { T, n, tau } = state;
    const sv = reactivity(T, f);
    const pFus = f.pair * n * n * sv * f.E;
    const pAlpha = f.fc * pFus;
    const pBrem = CBREM * n * n * Math.sqrt(Math.max(T, 0.001));
    const Tj = T * J_PER_KEV;
    const pCond = (3 * n * Tj) / tau;

    // A star is optically thick and gravitationally bound: its radiation is
    // reabsorbed, so bremsstrahlung is not a loss and it simply burns, stably,
    // regulated by its own thermostat. A lab plasma has neither luxury.
    const pLoss = state.gravity ? 0 : pBrem + pCond;
    const ignited = state.gravity || (pAlpha >= pLoss && pFus > 1);
    const ext = Math.max(pLoss - pAlpha, 0);
    const Q = state.gravity ? Infinity : ext > 0 ? pFus / ext : Infinity;

    const tripleProduct = n * T * tau;
    // τ needed to ignite at this T and n (from pAlpha = pBrem + 3nT/τ)
    const head = pAlpha - pBrem;
    const tauIgn = head > 0 ? (3 * n * Tj) / head : Infinity;
    const tripleThreshold = n * T * tauIgn;

    // mean time for one nucleus to find a partner and react
    const partner = f.pair === 0.5 ? n : n / 2;
    const waitSec = sv > 0 && partner > 0 ? 1 / (partner * sv) : Infinity;
    const waitYears = waitSec / (3.15576e7);

    return { sv, pFus, pAlpha, pBrem, pCond, pLoss, ignited, Q, tripleProduct, tripleThreshold, waitYears };
  }

  // --- plasma portrait -------------------------------------------------------

  type Ion = { x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number; sp: number };
  let ions: Ion[] = [];
  type Flash = { x: number; y: number; life: number; ang: number };
  let flashes: Flash[] = [];
  let simTime = 0;
  let flashClock = 0;
  let ignitedGlow = 0;

  const NSHOW = 170;
  function speciesCount() {
    return state.fuel === 'pp' ? 1 : 2;
  }
  function buildIons() {
    ions = [];
    const speed = visualSpeed();
    for (let i = 0; i < NSHOW; i++) {
      const a = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
      // a rough spread of speeds around the thermal value
      const s = speed * (0.4 + Math.random() * 1.2);
      ions.push({
        x: Math.random(),
        y: Math.random(),
        vx: Math.cos(a) * s,
        vy: Math.sin(a) * s,
        sp: Math.random() < 0.5 ? 0 : 1,
      });
    }
  }
  function visualSpeed() {
    // map temperature onto a watchable on-screen speed
    return 0.06 * Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.05, state.T / 15));
  }

  function build() {
    buildIons();
    flashes = [];
    simTime = 0;
    flashClock = 0;
    ignitedGlow = 0;
  }

  function step(dt: number) {
    const b = balance();
    const sp = visualSpeed();
    // confinement leakiness bleeds a little motion out through the walls; a
    // well-confined plasma bounces cleanly.
    for (const p of ions) {
      p.x += p.vx * dt;
      p.y += p.vy * dt;
      if (p.x < 0) { p.x = 0; p.vx = Math.abs(p.vx); }
      if (p.x > 1) { p.x = 1; p.vx = -Math.abs(p.vx); }
      if (p.y < 0) { p.y = 0; p.vy = Math.abs(p.vy); }
      if (p.y > 1) { p.y = 1; p.vy = -Math.abs(p.vy); }
      // relax speeds toward the current temperature so the slider feels live
      const cur = Math.hypot(p.vx, p.vy);
      const want = sp * (0.4 + (p.sp + 0.5) * 0.4 + 0.4);
      if (cur > 0) {
        const k = 1 + (want / cur - 1) * Math.min(1, dt * 3);
        p.vx *= k;
        p.vy *= k;
      }
    }

    // visual fusion events at a watchable rate tied to the real fusion power
    const rateVis =
      b.pFus > 1 ? Math.min(55, 2.6 * Math.log10(b.pFus)) : 0;
    flashClock += dt;
    const period = rateVis > 0 ? 1 / rateVis : 1e9;
    while (flashClock > period && rateVis > 0) {
      flashClock -= period;
      if (ions.length > 2) {
        const i = (Math.random() * ions.length) | 0;
        const p = ions[i];
        flashes.push({ x: p.x, y: p.y, life: 1, ang: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2 });
        if (flashes.length > 70) flashes.shift();
      }
    }

    for (let k = flashes.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      flashes[k].life -= dt * 2.2;
      if (flashes[k].life <= 0) flashes.splice(k, 1);
    }

    ignitedGlow += ((b.ignited ? 1 : 0) - ignitedGlow) * Math.min(1, dt * 2);
    simTime += dt;
  }

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('fus') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const D_COL = '#5b8cff';
  const T_COL = '#34d399';
  const FIRE = '#ffb03a';
  const HOT = '#ff6a5a';
  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const GOOD = '#34d399';
  const WARN = '#f59e0b';
  const BAD = '#ef4444';
  const DIM = '#8a8f9c';

  const BOX = { x: 20, y: 84, w: 592, h: 620 };
  const RX = { x: 632, y: 84, w: 348, h: 210 };
  const PB = { x: 632, y: 316, w: 348, h: 178 };
  const LAW = { x: 632, y: 512, w: 348, h: 192 };

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.arcTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + h, rad);
    ctx.arcTo(x + w, y + h, x, y + h, rad);
    ctx.arcTo(x, y + h, x, y, rad);
    ctx.arcTo(x, y, x + w, y, rad);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }

  function fuelColour(sp: number) {
    if (state.fuel === 'pp') return D_COL;
    return sp === 0 ? D_COL : T_COL;
  }

  function drawBox() {
    const b = balance();
    panel(BOX, 'THE PLASMA');
    const ix = BOX.x + 24, iy = BOX.y + 44, iw = BOX.w - 48, ih = BOX.h - 96;

    // a warm floor whose glow tracks how hard the plasma is burning
    const glow = ignitedGlow;
    const grd = ctx.createRadialGradient(
      ix + iw / 2, iy + ih / 2, 20,
      ix + iw / 2, iy + ih / 2, iw * 0.7
    );
    grd.addColorStop(0, `rgba(255,${150 - glow * 60},60,${0.05 + glow * 0.22})`);
    grd.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(255,120,40,0)');
    ctx.fillStyle = grd;
    ctx.fillRect(ix, iy, iw, ih);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(state.gravity ? 0.14 : 0.24);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    if (state.gravity) ctx.setLineDash([4, 5]);
    rr(ix, iy, iw, ih, 8);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    // ions
    for (const p of ions) {
      const x = ix + p.x * iw, y = iy + p.y * ih;
      ctx.fillStyle = fuelColour(p.sp);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 2.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }

    // fusion flashes with a little product streak
    for (const f of flashes) {
      const x = ix + f.x * iw, y = iy + f.y * ih;
      const a = Math.max(0, f.life);
      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(255,176,58,${a})`;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 3 + (1 - a) * 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(255,106,90,${a * 0.8})`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
      const r = (1 - a) * 22;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      ctx.lineTo(x + Math.cos(f.ang) * r, y + Math.sin(f.ang) * r);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // header readout
    label(`T = ${fmtTemp(state.T)}`, BOX.x + 6, BOX.y + 22, 0.85, 'left', 13, HOT);
    label(`n = ${eng(state.n, '/m³', 1)}`, BOX.x + BOX.w - 6, BOX.y + 22, 0.85, 'right', 13, ACC);

    // legend + confinement note along the bottom
    const ly = BOX.y + BOX.h - 14;
    if (state.fuel === 'pp') {
      dot(BOX.x + 10, ly - 4, D_COL);
      label('protons', BOX.x + 22, ly, 0.55, 'left', 11);
    } else {
      dot(BOX.x + 10, ly - 4, D_COL);
      label('deuterium', BOX.x + 22, ly, 0.55, 'left', 11);
      dot(BOX.x + 118, ly - 4, T_COL);
      label(state.fuel === 'dhe3' ? 'helium-3' : 'tritium', BOX.x + 130, ly, 0.55, 'left', 11);
    }
    dot(BOX.x + 250, ly - 4, FIRE);
    label('fusion', BOX.x + 262, ly, 0.55, 'left', 11);
    if (state.gravity)
      label('gravity holds it — radiation trapped', BOX.x + BOX.w - 6, ly, 0.5, 'right', 11, WARN);
    else
      label(`confinement τ = ${eng(state.tau, 's', 1)}`, BOX.x + BOX.w - 6, ly, 0.5, 'right', 11, DIM);
  }
  function dot(x: number, y: number, c: string) {
    ctx.fillStyle = c;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(x, y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
  }

  function drawReactivity() {
    panel(RX, 'REACTIVITY vs TEMPERATURE');
    const px = RX.x + 40, py = RX.y + 18, pw = RX.w - 56, ph = RX.h - 52;
    const f = FUELS[state.fuel];
    const Tmin = 0.3, Tmax = 300;
    const LX = (T: number) => px + (Math.log(T / Tmin) / Math.log(Tmax / Tmin)) * pw;
    // sample the curve to find its own vertical range
    const svMax = Math.max(reactivity(Tmax, f), 1e-30);
    const svFloor = 1e-30;
    const LY = (sv: number) =>
      py + ph - (Math.log(Math.max(sv, svFloor) / svFloor) / Math.log(svMax / svFloor)) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.22);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();

    // the reactivity curve for the current fuel
    ctx.strokeStyle = HOT;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let i = 0; i <= 120; i++) {
      const T = Tmin * Math.pow(Tmax / Tmin, i / 120);
      const x = LX(T), y = LY(reactivity(T, f));
      i ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    // where we are now
    const cx = LX(state.T), cy = LY(reactivity(state.T, f));
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.3);
    ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(cx, py);
    ctx.lineTo(cx, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.fillStyle = FIRE;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(cx, cy, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    for (const T of [1, 10, 100]) label(`${T}`, LX(T), py + ph + 15, 0.4, 'center', 9);
    label('keV', px + pw, py + ph + 15, 0.4, 'right', 9);
    label(`${f.label}`, px + 4, py + 12, 0.75, 'left', 12, HOT);
    label('almost vertical: fusion is fierce about temperature', px, RX.y + RX.h - 12, 0.4, 'left', 10);
  }

  function drawBalance() {
    const b = balance();
    panel(PB, 'POWER: OUT vs LOST');
    const px = PB.x + 16, pw = PB.w - 32;
    let y = PB.y + 26;

    if (state.gravity) {
      label('GRAVITY-CONFINED STAR', px, y, 0.95, 'left', 14, WARN);
      y += 22;
      label('radiation is trapped and reabsorbed, so it simply', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
      y += 16;
      label('burns at whatever rate its own weight allows', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
      y += 26;
      label(`fusion power ≈ ${eng(b.pFus, 'W/m³', 1)}`, px, y, 0.8, 'left', 13, FIRE);
      y += 22;
      label('less per litre than a warm compost heap,', px, y, 0.45, 'left', 11);
      y += 15;
      label('and yet it has shone for billions of years', px, y, 0.45, 'left', 11);
      return;
    }

    // two bars: alpha self-heating vs total loss, on a shared log scale
    const vals = [b.pAlpha, b.pLoss, 1];
    const top = Math.max(...vals) * 3;
    const bot = 1e-3;
    const BW = (v: number) =>
      Math.max(2, (Math.log(Math.max(v, bot) / bot) / Math.log(top / bot)) * pw);

    label('self-heating (α)', px, y, 0.55, 'left', 11, FIRE);
    label(eng(b.pAlpha, 'W/m³', 1), px + pw, y, 0.7, 'right', 11, FIRE);
    y += 8;
    ctx.fillStyle = FIRE;
    rr(px, y, BW(b.pAlpha), 12, 3);
    ctx.fill();
    y += 26;
    label('losses (radiation + leak)', px, y, 0.55, 'left', 11, ACC);
    label(eng(b.pLoss, 'W/m³', 1), px + pw, y, 0.7, 'right', 11, ACC);
    y += 8;
    ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
    rr(px, y, BW(b.pLoss), 12, 3);
    ctx.fill();
    y += 30;

    if (b.ignited) {
      label('IGNITED — the fire feeds itself', px, y, 0.95, 'left', 15, GOOD);
      y += 22;
      label('the alphas alone outheat every loss', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    } else {
      const qtxt = b.Q === Infinity ? '∞' : b.Q < 0.01 ? b.Q.toExponential(1) : b.Q.toFixed(2);
      label(`not igniting · gain Q = ${qtxt}`, px, y, 0.9, 'left', 14, b.Q > 1 ? WARN : DIM);
      y += 22;
      if (b.pAlpha <= b.pBrem)
        label('bremsstrahlung alone beats it — too cold', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11, DIM);
      else
        label('heat leaks out faster than fusion makes it', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11, DIM);
    }
  }

  function drawLawson() {
    const b = balance();
    panel(LAW, 'THE LAWSON LINE  (n · T · τ)');
    const px = LAW.x + 16, pw = LAW.w - 32;
    let y = LAW.y + 28;

    if (state.gravity) {
      label(`a proton here waits`, px, y, 0.6, 'left', 12);
      y += 24;
      label(fmtYears(b.waitYears), px, y, 0.95, 'left', 20, WARN);
      y += 26;
      label('to fuse. Only the Sun’s sheer size turns that', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
      y += 15;
      label('trickle into a star. Multiply this rate by 10⁵⁷', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
      y += 15;
      label('nuclei and you get a steady 4×10²⁶ watts.', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11);
      return;
    }

    const tp = b.tripleProduct;
    const thr = b.tripleThreshold;
    // a log bar from 1e18 to 1e24 keV·s/m³
    const lo = 1e18, hi = 1e24;
    const LX = (v: number) => px + (Math.log(Math.max(v, lo) / lo) / Math.log(hi / lo)) * pw;
    const barY = y + 6;
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
    rr(px, barY, pw, 14, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    const grd = ctx.createLinearGradient(px, 0, px + pw, 0);
    grd.addColorStop(0, DIM);
    grd.addColorStop(1, GOOD);
    ctx.fillStyle = grd;
    rr(px, barY, Math.max(3, LX(tp) - px), 14, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    // ignition threshold marker
    if (isFinite(thr) && thr > lo && thr < hi) {
      const tx = LX(thr);
      ctx.strokeStyle = GOOD;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(tx, barY - 5);
      ctx.lineTo(tx, barY + 19);
      ctx.stroke();
      label('ignition', tx, barY - 9, 0.6, 'center', 10, GOOD);
    }
    label('10¹⁸', px, barY + 30, 0.4, 'left', 9);
    label('10²⁴', px + pw, barY + 30, 0.4, 'right', 9);
    y = barY + 48;
    label(`n·T·τ = ${eng(tp, ' keV·s/m³', 1)}`, px, y, 0.85, 'left', 13, GOOD);
    y += 22;
    if (!isFinite(thr))
      label('no τ can ignite this — raise the temperature first', px, y, 0.5, 'left', 11, DIM);
    else if (tp >= thr)
      label('past the line: this plasma ignites', px, y, 0.6, 'left', 11, GOOD);
    else
      label('below the line: hotter, denser, or held longer', px, y, 0.55, 'left', 11, WARN);
  }

  // --- formatting ------------------------------------------------------------

  function fmtTemp(keV: number): string {
    const K = keV * KB_KEV_K;
    if (K >= 1e9) return `${keV.toFixed(0)} keV · ${(K / 1e9).toFixed(1)} bn K`;
    return `${keV < 1 ? keV.toFixed(2) : keV.toFixed(1)} keV · ${(K / 1e6).toFixed(0)} M K`;
  }
  function fmtYears(y: number): string {
    if (!isFinite(y)) return 'forever';
    if (y >= 1e9) return `${(y / 1e9).toFixed(1)} billion yr`;
    if (y >= 1e6) return `${(y / 1e6).toFixed(1)} million yr`;
    if (y >= 1) return `${y.toFixed(1)} yr`;
    const s = y * 3.15576e7;
    return eng(s, 's', 1);
  }
  function eng(x: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(x);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    if (a < 1e-3 || a >= 1e6) return `${x.toExponential(digits)}${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-3, 'm'], [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(x / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string, col?: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    const b = el('r' + n);
    b.textContent = val;
    if (col) b.style.color = col;
    else b.style.removeProperty('color');
  };
  const setEq = equationBar();
  function updateReadout() {
    const b = balance();
    setRow(1, 'Temperature', fmtTemp(state.T));
    setRow(2, 'Reactivity σv', `${b.sv.toExponential(1)} m³/s`);
    setRow(3, 'Fusion power', eng(b.pFus, 'W/m³', 1), FIRE);
    setRow(4, 'Wait per nucleus', fmtYears(b.waitYears));
    let st: string, col: string;
    if (state.gravity) { st = 'burning star'; col = WARN; }
    else if (b.ignited) { st = 'ignited'; col = GOOD; }
    else if (b.pFus > 1) { st = 'burning, not self-sustaining'; col = ACC; }
    else { st = 'cold — nothing fuses'; col = DIM; }
    setRow(5, 'State', st, col);
    setEq([
      [
        ['P_{\\text{fus}}', FIRE],
        '= n_D\\,n_T\\,\\langle\\sigma v\\rangle\\,E_{\\text{fus}}',
        '\\quad\\text{and }\\langle\\sigma v\\rangle\\text{ climbs steeply with }T',
      ],
      [
        `T = ${state.T < 1 ? state.T.toFixed(2) : state.T.toFixed(1)}\\,\\text{keV}`,
        `\\quad\\langle\\sigma v\\rangle = ${b.sv.toExponential(1)}\\,\\text{m}^3/\\text{s}`,
        [`\\quad P_{\\text{fus}} = \\text{${eng(b.pFus, 'W/m', 1)}}^3`, FIRE],
      ],
      [
        'nuclei have to tunnel through their own repulsion, which is why temperature matters so much',
      ],
    ]);
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Nuclear Fusion', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label('tunnel through the barrier, then beat the losses', 20, 52, 0.5, 'left', 11, GOOD);
    drawBox();
    drawReactivity();
    drawBalance();
    drawLawson();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dtReal = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dtReal = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dtReal));
    if (state.running) {
      const dt = dtReal * state.rate;
      step(dt);
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    build();
    state.running = true;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Pause';
  });

  // log-scaled sliders: slider 0..100 maps onto a physical value
  const T_MIN = 0.3, T_DEC = 3; // 0.3 .. 300 keV
  const N_MIN = 1e19, N_DEC = 14; // 1e19 .. 1e33 /m³
  const TAU_MIN = 1e-10, TAU_DEC = 15; // 1e-10 .. 1e5 s
  const fromSlider = (v: number, min: number, dec: number) =>
    min * Math.pow(10, (v / 100) * dec);
  const toSlider = (val: number, min: number, dec: number) =>
    (Math.log10(val / min) / dec) * 100;

  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.addEventListener('input', () => apply(+inp.value));
    apply(+inp.value);
  }
  bindRange('temp', (v) => {
    state.T = fromSlider(v, T_MIN, T_DEC);
    el('tval').textContent = fmtTemp(state.T);
  });
  bindRange('dens', (v) => {
    state.n = fromSlider(v, N_MIN, N_DEC);
    el('nval').textContent = eng(state.n, '/m³', 1);
  });
  bindRange('conf', (v) => {
    state.tau = fromSlider(v, TAU_MIN, TAU_DEC);
    el('tauval').textContent = eng(state.tau, 's', 1);
  });
  bindRange('rate', (v) => {
    state.rate = v / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });

  function setSlider(id: string, value: number) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.value = String(value);
    inp.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));
  }
  function setFuel(f: FuelKey) {
    state.fuel = f;
    document.querySelectorAll('#fuel button').forEach((b) =>
      b.classList.toggle('active', (b as HTMLElement).dataset.f === f)
    );
    buildIons();
  }

  el('fuel').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    setFuel(btn.dataset.f as FuelKey);
  });

  const SCENES: Record<Scenario, { fuel: FuelKey; T: number; n: number; tau: number; gravity: boolean }> = {
    cold: { fuel: 'dt', T: 0.5, n: 1e20, tau: 1, gravity: false },
    tokamak: { fuel: 'dt', T: 15, n: 1e20, tau: 3, gravity: false },
    sun: { fuel: 'pp', T: 1.3, n: 1e32, tau: 1e5, gravity: true },
    hbomb: { fuel: 'dt', T: 60, n: 3e31, tau: 1e-9, gravity: false },
  };

  function applyScene(s: Scenario) {
    state.scenario = s;
    const c = SCENES[s];
    state.gravity = c.gravity;
    setFuel(c.fuel);
    setSlider('temp', clampSlider(toSlider(c.T, T_MIN, T_DEC)));
    setSlider('dens', clampSlider(toSlider(c.n, N_MIN, N_DEC)));
    setSlider('conf', clampSlider(toSlider(c.tau, TAU_MIN, TAU_DEC)));
    build();
    state.running = true;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Pause';
  }
  const clampSlider = (v: number) => Math.max(0, Math.min(100, v));

  el('scenario').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#scenario button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    applyScene(btn.dataset.s as Scenario);
  });

  // any manual slider change means we are no longer strictly in the star regime
  for (const id of ['temp', 'dens', 'conf']) {
    el(id).addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (state.scenario !== 'sun') state.gravity = false;
    });
  }

  applyScene('cold');
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

